  "title": "The Time-Course of Food Representation in the Human Brain",
  "description": "This dataset comprises raw EEG recordings collected to investigate the time-course of food representation in the human brain. Participants viewed food-related stimuli while EEG was recorded, enabling analysis of temporal neural dynamics underlying food perception and categorization. The dataset supports research on visual object and food representation using time-resolved decoding approaches.",
  "methods_description": "EEG data were collected and organized according to the Brain Imaging Data Structure (BIDS) standard. Analysis code and associated figures are available through the Open Science Framework.",
